  "final": "`get_document` and `list_documents` now only return documents that match both tenant and owner and have `deleted_at IS NULL`. `checks/public.py` and my new `checks/security.py` both pass.\n\n- **`src/repository.py`:**\n  - `find` and `listing` now take `tenant` and `owner`, and both queries filter on tenant, owner and `deleted_at IS NULL`.\n  - Every value goes through `?` bound parameters.\n  - The result fields are still `id`, `title` and `body`, and the list is still ordered by `id`.\n- **`src/service.py`:** it now passes `tenant` through. Before, `get_document` ignored tenant and owner, and `list_documents` ignored tenant.\n- **Unavailable IDs:** `get_document` returns `None` for a missing, cross-tenant, cross-owner or deleted ID. It doesn't say which case applied.\n- **`checks/security.py`:**\n  - It checks that cross-tenant, cross-owner and deleted rows are hidden.\n  - It checks that list results contain only `id`, `title` and `body`, ordered by `id`.\n  - It checks that tenant and owner names containing quotes are handled safely, including injection-style strings.\n\n`find` and `listing` changed signature, but only `src/service.py` called them.",
