            "text": "{\"output\":\"import os, sys\\nsys.path.insert(0, os.getcwd())\\nimport sqlite3\\nfrom src.repository import initialize\\nfrom src.service import get_document, list_documents\\nc = sqlite3.connect(\\\":memory:\\\")\\ninitialize(c)\\nc.execute(\\\"INSERT INTO documents VALUES (1, 't', 'o', 'Title', 'Body', NULL)\\\")\\nc.commit()\\nassert get_document(c, \\\"t\\\", \\\"o\\\", 1) == {\\\"id\\\": 1, \\\"title\\\": \\\"Title\\\", \\\"body\\\": \\\"Body\\\"}\\nassert list_documents(c, \\\"t\\\", \\\"o\\\") == [{\\\"id\\\": 1, \\\"title\\\": \\\"Title\\\", \\\"body\\\": \\\"Body\\\"}]\\nassert get_document(c, \\\"t\\\", \\\"o\\\", 99) is None\\n# Service component\\n\\nSecure get_document(connection, tenant, owner, document_id) and list_documents in src/service.py. Only documents matching both tenant and owner and having deleted_at IS NULL are accessible. get_document returns None for any unavailable ID without distinguishing cross-tenant, cross-owner or deleted records. Lists return dictionaries ordered by id, and no deletion metadata. All queries use bound parameters, including names containing quotes. Keep result fields id, title and body unchanged. Start in src/service.py and src/repository.py.\\n\\nRun `python3 checks/public.py` from the project root. Implementation belongs in src/. Add checks under checks/.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"signal\":null,\"cancelled\":false,\"timeout\":false,\"truncated\":false}"
